## Copernicus Marine SST and Chlorophyll-a

The ocean agent takes SST and Chl-a grids from Copernicus Marine first, then from MOSDAC
(per field), and the fishing agent finds fronts in them (providers/copernicus.py).

  sst  METOFFICE-GLO-SST-L4-NRT-OBS-SST-V2                        (SST_GLO_SST_L4_NRT_OBSERVATIONS_010_001)
  chl  cmems_obs-oc_glo_bgc-plankton_nrt_l4-gapfree-multi-4km_P1D  (OCEANCOLOUR_GLO_BGC_L4_NRT_009_102)

Streaming (free account at https://data.marine.copernicus.eu):
  pip install -r requirements.txt
  copernicusmarine login        # or set COPERNICUSMARINE_SERVICE_USERNAME / COPERNICUSMARINE_SERVICE_PASSWORD

Offline, from downloaded files (set COPERNICUS_DATA_DIR to the folder):
  copernicusmarine subset -i METOFFICE-GLO-SST-L4-NRT-OBS-SST-V2 -v analysed_sst -x 66 -X 74 -y 17 -Y 24 -t 2026-09-20 -T 2026-09-26 -o data/cmems
  copernicusmarine subset -i cmems_obs-oc_glo_bgc-plankton_nrt_l4-gapfree-multi-4km_P1D -v CHL -x 66 -X 74 -y 17 -Y 24 -t 2026-09-20 -T 2026-09-26 -o data/cmems

Both products lag real time by about a day, so the provider uses the latest day with data
within COPERNICUS_LOOKBACK_DAYS (default 5) before the voyage window. The day used is shown
in the provider message and the observation timestamps.
